1
00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:39,333
One Last Dance is a romance, drama, music film directed by Lisa Niemi.

2
00:11:06,666 --> 00:11:12,666
In the wake of tragedy, a renowed New York dance
company is on the brink of collapse.

3
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:46,000
After leaving the dance world for good, Travis, Chrissa, and Max are
pulled in to resurrect the dance that shattered their careers.

4
00:22:13,333 --> 00:22:19,333
They have one last chance to save the company, re-connect with the
passion and magic, and prove that miracles really can happen.

5
00:27:46,666 --> 00:27:52,666
Travis MacPhearson, played by Patrick Swayze.

6
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Chrissa Lindh, played by Lisa Niemi.

7
00:38:53,333 --> 00:38:59,333
Max Delano, played by George De La Pena.

8
00:44:26,666 --> 00:44:32,666
Alex McGrath, played by Matthew Walker.

9
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Orest, played by Stefan Wenta.

10
00:55:33,333 --> 00:55:39,333
Jerry, played by Timothy Webber.

11
01:01:06,666 --> 01:01:12,666
One Last Dance is a 2003 American-Canadian romantic drama
film about three dancers in New York City.

12
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
The film was directed and written by Lisa Niemi, wife of actor Patrick Swayze.

13
01:12:13,333 --> 01:12:19,333
One Last Dance starred both Swayze and Niemi, who also jointly
produced, alongside George de la Peña in a major role.

14
01:17:46,666 --> 01:17:52,666
It was filmed in Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada.

15
01:23:20,000 --> 01:23:26,000
One Last Dance was choreographed by Patsy Swayze, Niemi's
mother-in-law and the mother of Patrick Swayze.

16
01:28:53,333 --> 01:28:59,333
Niemi, who also wrote the script in addition to directing the film, drew its content
from the real-life experiences and struggles of performing artists.

17
01:34:26,666 --> 01:34:32,666
The tone is emotional.
